      "plainText": "Paste samples for the docx4j editor\nEach numbered section below is one capture: select from its heading to the line before the next heading, copy, and save the clipboard HTML as paste/README.md says. The last capture is the whole document.\n1. Headings and body text\nA second-level heading\nBody text under the second-level heading, one plain sentence.\nA third-level heading\nBody text under the third-level heading, with a second sentence to make a longer paragraph that Word will wrap on its own.\n2. Inline formatting\nThis paragraph has bold, italic, underlined, struck through, a superscript and a subscript run, then bold italic together.\nA line break follows this text\nand this is the same paragraph after it, then a tab\tand text after the tab.\n3. A bulleted list\nFirst bullet\nSecond bullet\nA nested bullet under the second\nAnother nested bullet\nThird bullet, back at the first level\nA plain paragraph after the list.\n4. A numbered list\nFirst item\nSecond item\nA nested item under the second\nAnother nested item\nThird item, back at the first level\nA plain paragraph after the list.\n5. A simple table\nA three-by-three table with a header row:\nName\tQuantity\tPrice\nWidget\t2\t3.50\nGadget\t10\t12.00\nA plain paragraph after the table.\n6. What the editor drops on paste\nThis paragraph is centred, indented and in 14-point red Arial; the editor keeps the text and drops the rest, and says so.\nThis one has a highlighted word.\n",
